-- title:
--   W[[X]]/(X-varpi^e) is a discrete valuation ring
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, let $\varpi \in W$ be an irreducible element, and let $e$ be a natural number with $1 \le e$. Consider the principal ideal of the one-variable power series ring $W[\![X]\!]$ generated by $X - C(\varpi^e)$, where $C$ denotes the inclusion of constants. The theorem asserts four things simultaneously: this ideal is prime; the quotient ring $D = W[\![X]\!]/(X - \varpi^e)$ is a principal ideal ring; $D$ is a local ring; and the image in $D$ of the constant power series $\varpi$ is an irreducible element of $D$. Together these say that $D$ is a local principal ideal domain whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\varpi$ — that is, a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser the image of $\varpi$, in which the image of $X$ equals the $e$-th power of that uniformiser. The statement is phrased entirely in terms of primality, principality, locality and irreducibility rather than asserting the discrete valuation ring property itself.
--
--   The ring $D$ is canonically the $\varpi$-adic completion of $W$, realised without mentioning completions; it is the coefficient ring that appears when the crossing local model $W[\![u,v]\!]/(uv - \varpi^e)$ over a possibly non-complete discrete valuation ring is analysed, and it is used in the computation of stalks and completions for the crossing scheme and in the accompanying results on surjections from power series rings and on integral closedness of such local rings.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PowerSeries_quotient_span_X_sub_C_pow_of_irreducible.lean

